From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Treggat <taggert2222@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 05:10:01 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 22/27] llama/server/sycl : less host traffic in prefill,
 lighter checkpoints

Exact host-side changes for prefill with an MTP draft context, behind
env switches (default off):
- LLAMA_MTP_H_DEVICE: the MTP hidden-state rows stay on the device
  instead of a download and re-upload per ubatch
- LLAMA_KQ_MASK_HINT_NOFILL: skip the host fill of a tagged causal mask
- LLAMA_KV_CKPT_PARTIAL_SKIP: a draft context checkpoint no longer
  copies the whole draft KV; the tail is trimmed with seq_rm
- LLAMA_CKPT_POOL: reuse checkpoint buffers
Diagnostics: GGML_SYCL_FA_STATS (kernel and mask-tag counters; =2
re-runs every causal attention call on the explicit-mask path and
compares bit for bit), GGML_SYCL_GPU_TIMELINE, more LLAMA_HOST_PROF
keys, PPL_STREAM=1 for llama-perplexity.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
